{{ define "about" }}
    {{ template "base" . }}
{{ end }}

{{ define "title" }}mums | About{{ end }}

{{ define "content" }}
    <div class="self-center max-w-full flex flex-col items-center gap-6">

        <hgroup class="flex flex-col items-center gap-2 w-full">
            <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-backdrop-content">
                mums
            </h1>

            <p class="text-lg text-backdrop-content-muted">
                Serving beverages since 1337!
            </p>
        </hgroup>

        <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 w-full text-sm leading-relaxed text-backdrop-content">
            <p>
                <strong>mums</strong> is a web application designed to easily track and manage
                <em>mums</em> throughout the introductory period.
            </p>

            <p>
                This project is built with simplicity at its core, deliberately avoiding the
                build steps that are common in modern web development. It combines
                {{ template "component-external-link" dict
                    "Href" "https://htmx.org/"
                    "Class" "font-semibold text-backdrop-content-highlight"
                    "Text" "HTMX"
                }} and {{ template "component-external-link" dict
                    "Href" "https://tailwindcss.com/"
                    "Class" "font-semibold text-backdrop-content-highlight"
                    "Text" "Tailwind CSS"
                }} on the frontend with
                {{ template "component-external-link" dict
                    "Href" "https://echo.labstack.com/"
                    "Class" "font-semibold text-backdrop-content-highlight"
                    "Text" "Echo"
                }} and {{ template "component-external-link" dict
                    "Href" "https://www.sqlite.org/"
                    "Class" "font-semibold text-backdrop-content-highlight"
                    "Text" "SQLite"
                }} on the backend to create a lightweight
                server-driven architecture.
            </p>

            <p>
                Nearly everything above the framework is built in-house: session management with
                sliding expiry, role-based access control for both user accounts and per-group
                roles, password-reset and invite tokens, the database access layer (plain SQL, no
                ORM), and a database event bus that streams live page updates over SSE.
            </p>

            <p>
                The dependencies are intentionally kept few and minimal, with no scaffolding or
                code generation, so every layer stays small and readable, making the setup easy to
                run and maintain.
            </p>
        </div>

    </div>
{{ end }}
